{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/31613-historical-h-tv","id":31613,"title":"Historical H:tV","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-17T06:34:29-08:00","id":31613,"title":"Historical H:tV","content":"After my Savage Worlds burnout, I've been looking for a system that could do Solomon Kane-style cloak-and-sword-and-sorcery historical horror with swashbucklers facing supernatural foes.<br /> <br /> I discarded the myriad D&amp;D-based offerings as well as BRP/CoC, systems that I love well enough, because of their built-in assumptions.<br /> <br /> Now I'm thinking of using Storytelling/nWoD because, well, that would essentially amount to a historical Hunter: The Vigil game. And there's no shortage of supernatural baddies.<br /> <br /> Has anyone ever ran a historical Vigil game? What time and place did you pick? How did it turn out? Any tricks, tips, pitfalls to avoid?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1714-the-butcher","name":"The Butcher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T07:30:46-08:00","id":31650,"title":"","content":"I played in a Victorian England Hunter game where we investigated, searched for, and fought Jack the Ripper. It was awesome. One of the reasons I'm so excited about Dark Eras, and the Hunter aspect of it, is that I feel that Hunter is a game that works well under any setting.<br /> <br /> Having a group of Hunters search out a killer in Ancient Rome, or even the Wild West is something that appeals to me. Hunter the Vigil(and Reckoning following it) is my favorite game line. The fact that it works well under any time period and/or constraint is part of that.<br /> <br /> Like you said, no shortage of supernatural baddies...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}